/*!
\page page_stEmcDetector StEmcDetector

\brief One sub-detector plane of the STAR Electromagnetic Calorimeter.

\section emcdetector_overview Overview

StEmcDetector is the top-level container for one EMC sub-detector (e.g. the
BEMC tower layer, the BEMC pre-shower, an SMD plane, or an EEMC layer).  It
owns an array of up to 120 StEmcModule objects holding raw hits, an
StEmcClusterCollection for reconstructed clusters, and an array of crate
status flags.

\section emcdetector_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StEmcDetector
\endcode

Accessed via \ref page_stEmcCollection "StEmcCollection".

\section emcdetector_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| StDetectorId | mDetectorId | Sub-detector identifier (e.g. kBarrelEmcTowerId). |
| UInt_t | mNumberOfModules | Number of active readout modules (up to 120). |
| StEmcModule*[120] | mModules | Array of owned module objects (1-based). |
| StEmcClusterCollection* | mClusters | Owned cluster collection. |
| StEmcCrateStatus[36] | mCrateStatusFlag | Health flags for each readout crate. |

\section emcdetector_methods Key Methods

- \c detectorId() — sub-detector identifier.
- \c numberOfModules() — number of active modules.
- \c addHit(StEmcRawHit*) — route a hit to the correct module.
- \c numberOfHits() — total hit count.
- \c getEnergy() — total energy sum [GeV].
- \c module(uint) — access a module by 1-based index.
- \c cluster() — access the cluster collection.
- \c crateStatus(int) — crate health flag.
- \c setCluster(), \c setModule(), \c setCrateStatus() — setters.

\section emcdetector_seealso See Also

\ref page_stEmcModule "StEmcModule",
\ref page_stEmcRawHit "StEmcRawHit",
\ref page_stEmcCluster "StEmcCluster"
*/
